Subject: CK: backport of ROCm/rocm-libraries#13395 (FMHA forward max logits)

The library part of https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-libraries/pull/13395 (include/ck_tile and the
01_fmha codegen and API; PR head 63df9a77b9), ported to AITER's CK. Drop this patch once AITER's
CK includes that PR.

Adds fmha_fwd_args::max_logits_ptr: fp32, same layout as the LSE, sink excluded, -inf for fully
masked rows. qr, qr_async and qr_async_trload track the exact max logits when the
kStoreMaxLogits trait is set. Codegen adds _max_logits instances for gfx9/gfx950 (receipts 0 and
700), which the dispatch picks only when max_logits_ptr is set; existing instances are unchanged.

Differences from the PR diff, due to the older CK: two hunks of fmha_fwd_kernel.hpp (the kernel
static_assert and the IsSupportedArgument check) were placed by hand, and codegen/ops/fmha_fwd.py
also imports dataclasses.replace, which the PR's base already imported.

